&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Legal Ops Associate, OC Management on the Legal Operations team, you&#39;ll build and run the systems and processes that power Coinbase&#39;s outside counsel spend and management program. This team drives operational excellence across the Legal department by leveraging technology, automation, and AI-first workflows to manage vendors, budgets, and e-billing at scale. You&#39;ll partner closely with the Sr. Manager, Outside Counsel Spend &amp;amp; Strategy to optimize how Coinbase engages, evaluates, and pays outside counsel, directly impacting cost efficiency and program effectiveness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enhance automated, AI-first processes for legal e-billing and outside counsel management, driving operational excellence across the program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive implementation of OC spend strategy, including reviewing and benchmarking law firm billing rates and fee structures against industry standards and peer companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monthly accruals process and legal vendor onboarding workflows, ensuring accuracy and timeliness in close partnership with FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and maintain the legal e-billing system (Brightflag), serving as the team&#39;s resource for system optimization and stakeholder training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze OC spend data to produce reports, scorecards, and actionable insights that inform program improvements and leadership decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with FP&amp;amp;A, Sourcing, and EAA to enhance program effectiveness and align on budgets, forecasting, and vendor strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage onboarding of law firms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree with 3+ years of outside counsel management experience at an in-house legal practice, preferably at a high-growth technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing legal accruals, forecasting inputs, and month-end financial processes in partnership with FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with legal e-billing platforms (Brightflag or comparable) and proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets, including formulas, data manipulation, reconciliation, and building trackers and analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to project manage operational initiatives from inception to execution, including process design, tool implementation, and vendor onboarding workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data tools (SQL, Snowflake, Looker, or similar) for building reports and dashboards that drive spend visibility and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
